+-When a confidence gate fails (under deferred review: on anything but the fixed list the panel settles, §3), a run limit is hit (iterations, wall-clock, budget, pause flag), or a risk-list item is touched (auth, data migrations, money movement, production config), the run **parks**: it finishes every artifact it can, writes a "what I need from you" section into the PR description, records the reason in `status.yaml`, labels the PR `sdlc:needs-human`, and notifies nobody. Parked and finished work waits in the review queue. The owner un-parks by settling the item on the PR (decision 24): a "Request changes" review (→ the fix round), or one of three labels — `sdlc:accept-risk` (accepts the risk-list hits the last gate reported), `sdlc:reset-iterations` (the fix-iteration and panel-call counts back to 0 after either cap), `sdlc:unlock-tests` (thaws the test-file lock of a fix-type change). Each label starts the fix round, which performs it, records the label's actor in `status.yaml` (`risk_accepted_by`, `iterations_reset_by` with its stamp `iterations_reset_at`, `tests_unlocked_by`), removes the label from the PR (one application is one act) and re-runs the phase; a label applied by the automation identity or a `[bot]` is rejected and left where it is, and the gate's `owner_actions` check re-judges the recorded actor. The gate believes a recorded actor that is a person, and the session can write `status.yaml`, so in CI the runner (`ci/run_phase.py`, loaded from the pinned framework checkout the session cannot edit) is the check (since 0.2.26, choice 103): it reads the owner-only fields right before the `claude -p` session — its own label handling included — and again right after, and a `risk_accepted_by`, `tests_unlocked_by` or `iterations_reset_by` entry the session added that the runner did not record and the default branch's copy does not carry, or an `iterations` or `panel_calls` count lower than before the session, restores the fields to their pre-session values a